    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen starting Neovim (no file, no plugins, --clean), the string +q4D73 appears on screen, typically overwriting or prepending to the welcome screen. This happens on terminals that do not support the Kitty / Progressive Enhancement Keyboard Protocol, specifically QTerminal.\n\nCaptured with:\nstrace -f -s 8192 -e trace=write,writev -o /tmp/nvim_strace.txt nvim --clean\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nopen qterminal(it is lxqt default terminal)\nnvim --clean\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe DCS probe is either:\n\n- Not sent to terminals that have not declared keyboard-protocol support (see DA response below), or\n- Garned output is zero — i.e. the terminal silently discards the DCSI payload.\n\nIn either case, no visible characters should appear.\n\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.12.5\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nyes\n\n### Operating system/version\n\narchlinux 7.1.11-arch1-1\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nqterminal 2.4.0\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\npacman -S neovim",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "In the UI startup sequence, before emitting the DCS + q … ST keyboard-protocol probe, check whether the terminal has advertised support (e.g. via the DA response or an explicit CSI ? u / Kitty KB CSI < u query). If not, skip the probe entirely.\n\nAlternatively / additionally, wrap the probe in a time-bounded \"wait for DCR / terminal response\" and only proceed if a response is received.",
