            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Can't check too deeply right now, but I'm not sure how this has anything to do with kitty keyboard protocol. Was that something AI told you? This looks like a duplicate of https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/40988.\n\nWorkaround:\n```lua\nlocal termfeatures = vim.g.termfeatures or {}\ntermfeatures.osc52 = false\nvim.g.termfeatures = termfeatures\n```\n\nI think it's caused by the fact that the terminal isn't ignoring unrecognized DCS sequences as it should when we query for OSC 52 support. We should probably document clearly somewhere the basic sequences that terminals should support, similar to how [fish does](https://github.com/fish-shell/fish-shell/blob/93bdb818247d02ab0197655f63eda880cee2bab4/doc_src/terminal-compatibility.rst):\n\n> If a valid CSI, OSC or DCS sequence does not represent a command implemented by the terminal, the terminal must ignore it.\n\nEdit: If you want to avoid similar problems in the future, I'd recommend using a modern, full-featured, highly compatible terminal like Ghostty or Kitty.",
